    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0662" n="530" xml:id="pg530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 369<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-07">July 7, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. The agreed recommendations submitted for your concurrence in Pauley’s 2441, July 6,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d369-f1"/> are in full conformity with the principles formulated in
                    the instructions to Pauley prepared by
                    the Informal Policy Committee on Germany, cleared with JCS and approved by the President. Pauley’s success in obtaining agreement of his Russian and
                    British colleagues represents a considerable achievement. It is recommended that
                    you communicate to Pauley your
                    concurrence and gratification.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
